Yesterday time taken by Vani to finish the work = 300/15 = 20 Today she is 40% faster i.e. 140% as efficient as the other day Today time taken by her to finish the work = 20/(140%) = (20 ×100)/140 ≅ 14min The required difference = 20 – 14 = 6 min SHORTCUT METHOD: Applying the same formula X = 300/15 = 20 K = (100 + 40)% = 140/100 = 1.4 So today Vani can finish the work in 20/(1.4 ) ≅14 days Required difference = 20 – 14 = 6 min
