In this statement:

This sounds like something best determined by testing.

Youâ€™ve got wheel deformation to deal with, surface deformation, and wheel/surface contact friction just off the top of my head. This is to say nothing about drivetrain losses, gearing, chains, shaft/bearing friction, etc.

Also, the difference between straight line resistance and turning friction needs to be accounted for as the wheel scrubs/slides/twists on the playing surface.

In short, these are some very complex issuesâ€¦ but on the good side, they can be measured experimentally fairly easily.

