Most basic physics courses just gloss over rolling friction by stating that it is very complicated and then simplifying it to be directly proportional to the normal force (if they even discuss rolling friction.)

This treatment is fine for a basic application that is making many other assumptions, but masks the underlying factors. Iâ€™ve used the video below in class as it does a good job of exploring the underlying issues with lots of visuals in a brief 5 minutes. Iâ€™d recommend watching it if you are interested in Rolling Friction (aka rolling resistance) and checking out some of LESICS videos on other topics too.

