# Chapter 11 - Additional Topics - 11.3 - Fractional Exponents - Problem Set 11.3 - Page 489: 53

#### Answer

$a^{\frac{17}{12}}$

#### Work Step by Step

Recall the following rule: $a^{n}+a^{m}=a^{n+m}$ Thus, we obtain: $a^{\frac{2}{3}}\times a^{\frac{3}{4}}$ =$a^{\frac{2}{3}+\frac{3}{4}}$ =$a^{\frac{2(4)+3(3)}{12}}$ =$a^{\frac{8+9}{12}}$ =$a^{\frac{17}{12}}$

