Chapter: Problem:

Business and Finance The closing prices for Kellogg Company stock are shown during the same 2-week period in 2003 as the Adobe Systems data in exercise 37.

 ADBE (Adobe Systems) DatePrice 2/3 2/4 2/5 2/6 2/7 2/10 2/11 2/12 2/13 2/14 32.32 32.53 32.33 32.24 32.10 32.12 31.50 31.30 31.21 31.65 Source: Yahoo! Finance

(a) Construct a box-and-whisker plot for the Kellogg Company closing stock price data.

(b) Describe any distinctive features shown by the plot.

(c) Compare your plot with the one constructed in exercise 37.

STEP-BY-STEP SOLUTION:
Chapter: Problem:
• Step 1 of 5

a.To construct a box-and-whisker plot, we first need to find the five-number summary. The five-number summary associated with a data set is given by:

Min, Q1, Median, Q3, Max

The smallest number is 31.21, so 31.21 is the min. The largest number is 32.53, so 32.53 is the max.

Next we need to find the median. .

Step 1: Rewrite the numbers in order from smallest to largest.

31.21, 31.30, 31.50, 31.65, 32.10, 32.12, 32.24, 32.32, 32.33, 32.53

Step 2: Count from both ends to find the number in the middle. Counting from both ends, we find that there are two numbers in the middle, 32.10 and 32.12. The median is the mean of these two numbers.

Now we need to find the first and third quartiles, Q1 and Q3.

31.21, 31.30, 31.50, 31.65, 32.10 are all to the left of the median.  Counting from both ends, we find that 31.50 is the median of this list, which is the first quartile.

Q1 = 31.50

32.12, 32.24, 32.32, 32.33, 32.53 are all to the right of the median.  Counting from both ends, we find that 32.32 is the median of this list, which is the third quartile.

Q3 = 32.32

The five-number summary for this set is

31.21, 31.50, 32.11, 32.32, 32.53

