# 10 imperial pints in metric teaspoons

## Conversion

10 imperial pints is equivalent to 1136.5225 metric teaspoons.[1]

## Conversion formula How to convert 10 imperial pints to metric teaspoons?

We know (by definition) that: $1\mathrm{imperialpint}\approx 113.65225\mathrm{brteaspoon}$

We can set up a proportion to solve for the number of metric teaspoons.

$1 ⁢ imperialpint 10 ⁢ imperialpint ≈ 113.65225 ⁢ brteaspoon x ⁢ brteaspoon$

Now, we cross multiply to solve for our unknown $x$:

$x\mathrm{brteaspoon}\approx \frac{10\mathrm{imperialpint}}{1\mathrm{imperialpint}}*113.65225\mathrm{brteaspoon}\to x\mathrm{brteaspoon}\approx 1136.5225\mathrm{brteaspoon}$

Conclusion: $10 ⁢ imperialpint ≈ 1136.5225 ⁢ brteaspoon$

## Conversion in the opposite direction

The inverse of the conversion factor is that 1 metric teaspoon is equal to 0.000879876993196351 times 10 imperial pints.

It can also be expressed as: 10 imperial pints is equal to $\frac{1}{\mathrm{0.000879876993196351}}$ metric teaspoons.

## Approximation

An approximate numerical result would be: ten imperial pints is about one thousand, one hundred and thirty-six point five one metric teaspoons, or alternatively, a metric teaspoon is about zero times ten imperial pints.

## Footnotes

[1] The precision is 15 significant digits (fourteen digits to the right of the decimal point).

Results may contain small errors due to the use of floating point arithmetic.

# "Two years later a father will be 8 years more than three times the age of the son "Taking the present age of father and son as x and y respectively. Write a linear equation for teh above.Find the age of the father when son is 10 years old

