## Intermediate Algebra: Connecting Concepts through Application

$-1,\frac{1}{4},\frac{-1}{9},\frac{1}{16},\frac{-1}{25}$
$a_n=\frac{(-1)^n}{n^2}$ $a_1=\frac{(-1)^1}{1^2}=-1$ $a_2=\frac{(-1)^2}{2^2}=\frac{1}{4}$ $a_3=\frac{(-1)^3}{3^2}=\frac{-1}{9}$ $a_4=\frac{(-1)^4}{4^2}=\frac{1}{16}$ $a_5=\frac{(-1)^5}{5^2}=\frac{-1}{25}$

Question

# Find the supplementary angles corresponding to all the angles of a right angle isosceles triangle [2 MARKS]

Solution

## Steps: 1 Mark Answer: 1 Mark The angles of a right-angled isosceles triangle are: 90∘, 45∘  and  45∘. Hence the supplementary angles are: 180∘−90∘=90∘ 180∘−45∘=135∘ 180∘−45∘=135∘

