## wattage calculator

How do you use the wattage calculator? To use this calculator, simply click on the apliances you want to power with the generator then enter the number of appliances you want to power, for example, if you want to run 2 window AC the you will have to put 2 in the window AC field. The calculator will then provide you with generators watts that will meet you home.

How do you calculate the power factor? AC power is equal to the current I in amps multiplied by the voltage V in volts multiplied by power factor divided by 1000. Power factor is the ratio between real powers to apparent power. V = Voltage. I = Current. PF = Power factor. Ac three-phase amps to kW conversion formula are similar to AC single phase but power factor value is changed.

What is the formula for watts? The formula for watts is W = I x E.CommentThe symbol for electric current is I; the symbol for ampere is A. The symbol for voltage is E, V, or U, depending upon context, and the symbol for volt is V. The symbol for power is P, and the symbol for watt is W.

How do you convert amps to watts? The formula for converting amps to watts (at a fixed voltage) is watts = amps × volts. To convert amps to watts you multiply your amps figure by the voltage. Note: conversions are a guide only. Note: conversions are a guide only. The Watt’s Law formula is all that’s needed for these unit conversions.

## What are you measuring when you measure in Watts?

