14-3(x+9)=5

ManuelBautista2019  Nov 6, 2017
Sort:

#1
+78756
+4

14 - 3(x+9) = 5     distribute the 3 across the terms in the parentheses

14 - 3x - 27   =  5

14 - 27  - 3x  =  5

-13   - 3x  =   5  add 13 to both sides

-3x  =  18       divide both sides by -3

x  =   -6

CPhill  Nov 6, 2017
#2
+499
+1

14-3(x+9)=5

Subtract 14 from both sides.

14-3(x+9)-14=5-14

Simplify

-3(x+9)=-9

Divide both sides by -3

Simplify

x+9-9=3-9

Subtract 9 from both sides

x+9-9=3-9

Simplify

x=-6

