If the eqn ax2+bx+c=0  (0 <a<b<c) has non real complex roots Z1 and Z2

then z1 & Z2 must be conjugate complex number.

and b2-4ac<0

and |Z1|= |Z2|

so i f  i will prove for one root then it is also true for other root

z1,z2={-b±i√(4ac-b2)}/2a

|z1|=√{b2 +(√(4ac-b2))2}/2a

|z1|=√{b2+4ac-b2}/2a

=√(c/a) >1

so |Z1|= |Z2| >1

