Example 4.8 A balanced three-phase star-connected load of 8 + j6 Ω per phase is supplied by a 400 V, 50 Hz supply. Calculate the line current, power factor, active, and reactive power.

Solution:

For star connection,

IPh = IL = 23.1 A

Angle of lag of IPh with VPh is 37°

Power factor                            = cos ϕ = cos 37° = 0.8 lagging

Active power                            = VL IL cos ϕ

= 1.732 × 400 × 23.1 × 0.8
= 12802 W = 12.802 kW

Reactive power                          = VL IL sin ϕ

= 1.732 × 400 × 23.1 × 0.6
= 9602 VAR = 9.602 kVAR

Example 4.9 A delta-connected three-phase motor load is supplied from a 400 V, thee-phase, 50 Hz supply system. The line current drawn is 21 A. The input power is 11 kW. What will be the line current and power factor when the motor windings are delta connected?

Solution:

Line voltage, VL = 400 V, VPh = VL for delta connection

Line current,                           IL = IPh = 21A

Impedance of each winding,

P = VL IL cos ϕ = ×400×21×cos ϕ

or,

