In star connection, the line current is the same as phase current, hence, IL = IPh = 7 A.

Power factor, depends on the circuit parameters

Since both R and Z remain unchanged, the power factor will remain the same at 0.756. Students may note that line current in a star connection is one-third of the line current in a delta connection.

Example 4.10 A balanced star-connected load of 4 + j6 Ω per phase is connected across a 400 V, three-phase, 50 Hz supply. Calculate line current, phase current, line voltage, phase voltage, power factor, total power, and reactive power.

Solution:

For star connection,

Power factor,                                     cos ϕ = cos 56° = 0.56 lagging

IPh = 32 A
