Example 4.16 The power input to a three-phase motor is measured by two single-phase wattmeters. The total input power has been measured as equal to 15 kW and the power factor calculated as 0.5. What have been the readings of the two wattmeters?

Solution:

Total power = W1 + W2 = 15 kW

We have to calculate W1 and W2

When we measure three-phase power by the two-wattmeter method, the readings of the two wattmeters are

W1 = VL IL cos (30 – ϕ)

and                                              W2 = VL IL cos (30 + ϕ)

