I think you have a typo the first term in the series should be $\displaystyle \displaystyle \frac{1}{2}$

$\displaystyle \displaystyle \frac{2}{x+3}=\frac{2}{4+(x-1)}=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{1+\frac{x-1}{4}} \right)=\frac{1}{2}\left(\frac{1}{1-\frac{-(x-1)}{4}} \right)$

Now this is in the form

$\displaystyle \displaystyle \frac{1}{1-r},r=\frac{-(x-1)}{4}$

So this is a geometric series and converges when $\displaystyle |r|<1$

