• The only difference between your two answers is that you exclude 0 whereas the website includes (correctly) 0. Since 0^2 = 0 and the square root of 0 is 0, the
Message 1 of 2 , Jan 2, 2011
View Source
The only difference between your two answers is that you exclude 0 whereas the website includes (correctly) 0. Since 0^2 = 0 and the square root of 0 is 0, the left side of the equation works out to 0. The right side is also 0 since -0 = 0. Thus, 0 works. (For what it's worth, I assume you mean to use interval notation so that, for example, (2,8] represents all real numbers strictly greater than 2 and less than or equal to 8, and I assume by "inf" you actually mean negative infinity.)

