Solution:

(b) $\frac{-4}{5}$

We ahve:

$\left(\frac{-5}{4}\right)^{-1}$

$=\frac{1}{\left(\frac{-5}{4}\right)}$

$=1 \times \frac{4}{-5}$

$=\frac{4}{-5}$

$=\frac{4 \times-1}{-5 \times-1}$

$=\frac{-4}{5}$

