## 33400

33,400 (thirty-three thousand four hundred) is an even five-digits composite number following 33399 and preceding 33401. In scientific notation, it is written as 3.34 × 104. The sum of its digits is 10. It has a total of 6 prime factors and 24 positive divisors. There are 13,280 positive integers (up to 33400) that are relatively prime to 33400.

## Basic properties

• Is Prime? No
• Number parity Even
• Number length 5
• Sum of Digits 10
• Digital Root 1

## Name

Short name 33 thousand 400 thirty-three thousand four hundred

## Notation

Scientific notation 3.34 × 104 33.4 × 103

## Prime Factorization of 33400

Prime Factorization 23 × 52 × 167

Composite number
Distinct Factors Total Factors Radical ω(n) 3 Total number of distinct prime factors Ω(n) 6 Total number of prime factors rad(n) 1670 Product of the distinct prime numbers λ(n) 1 Returns the parity of Ω(n), such that λ(n) = (-1)Ω(n) μ(n) 0 Returns: 1, if n has an even number of prime factors (and is square free) −1, if n has an odd number of prime factors (and is square free) 0, if n has a squared prime factor Λ(n) 0 Returns log(p) if n is a power pk of any prime p (for any k >= 1), else returns 0

The prime factorization of 33,400 is 23 × 52 × 167. Since it has a total of 6 prime factors, 33,400 is a composite number.

