#### mathemagister

Can $$\displaystyle \frac{3+x}{3}$$ be simplified to $$\displaystyle \frac{x}{3}$$
No, because $$\displaystyle \frac{3+x}{3} = \frac{3}{3}+\frac{x}{3} = 1 + \frac{x}{3}$$.

You can't just get rid of the 3 in the numerator.

