Okay but I am not looking for Force or Mass though.

There a couple of kinematics equations that will help you. I highly suggest memorizing these (there are a few others that definitely worth memorizing too).

Assuming a constant acceleration,

$$s = \frac{v_f + v_i}{2}t + s_i$$

and

$$s = \frac{1}{2}at^2 +v_it +s_i$$

(In many problems, $$s_i$$ is zero. And often times, either $$v_i$$ or $$v_f$$ is zero. But it doesn't hurt to memorize them in their full form.)

: These equations might be in a slightly different form in your textbook (or your instructors notes). In order to stay consistent with the class material, I suggest using textbook's (or your instructor's) notation.

