### Show Tags

27 Jan 2006, 02:28
I think D.

Say all number are (75+a, 75+b, 75+c, 75+d, 75+e, 75+f)

St1: This means a+b+c+d+e+f = 0 where all of them are greater than equal to zero. Only possible when all are zero. So all six number should be 75. SUFF

St2: This means a+b+c+d+e+f = 0 where all of them are less than equal to zero. Only possible when all are zero. So all six number should be 75. SUFF
