As we learnt in

Power dissipated in external resistance -

$P=(\frac{E}{R+r})^{2}R$

-

Total energy required = m s $\Delta$T

= 1000 $\times$ 1 cal/g $\times$ 80

= 80000 $\times$ 4.2 J = 336000J

$\therefore time \ required = \frac{energy}{power}= \frac{33600}{VI}$

$=\frac{33600}{220\times4}=6.3\ min$

Option 1)

6.4 minutes

Incorrect

